    "notes": "One part (Piano) with 2 staves (must not be split), Ab major, 8 bars of 4/4, 2 systems.  Chromatic chords with up to three stacked accidentals in one chord (e.g. bar 2 E-major triad: E natural, G#, B natural; bar 5 B-major triad), double flats and double sharps inside chords (Bbb4, Fb5 in bar 4; F##5 in bar 6; Bbb5 in bar 7), a natural-sharp in a chord (bar 6 F#5 after F##5), octave doublings in the left hand that need one accidental per octave, accidentals carried within the bar inside chords (bar 3), parenthesised courtesy accidentals in a chord (bar 5: Bb4, F5) and an unparenthesised courtesy flat (bar 8 Eb5).  Chords must stay chords (one <chord/> group per stem)."
